{
 "about": "Zeus purchase lock store table. Patterns are Python regexes, matched case-insensitively. Button labels are normalised first (lower case, money amounts and punctuation removed, spaces collapsed) and must match a label pattern as a WHOLE, so 'Place order' matches but 'Purchase history' does not. 'strong' labels are a purchase button on any page of a store below (and on any checkout page); 'weak' labels count only on a checkout page. Store ids match zeus-login: walmart amazon samsclub southwest ralphs. A store with a 'booking' block is a booking store: on its final review / purchase page the lock also reads the trip (flight numbers, the date of each flight, times, airport codes, passenger names and count, fare, refund words) and a press passes only when they match the trip in the owner's yes. Only booking kind 'flight' has a checker; any other kind fails closed. All booking patterns are general knowledge of Southwest's pages, not read off the real site (unverified).",
